# session.script — full seeded session (Q13 reference): help -> play -> deaths
# -> hi-score -> quit. Seed 12345, NUL-format fixture hi-score file.
#
# Boundary semantics under the quiescence handshake: during play a boundary
# ticks per VISIBLE frame completion (distinct rendered state, settled), so
# targets are effectively frame indices; on static screens (help/hi-score) an
# idle escape ticks them on a timer instead. See script-format.md.
#
# Authoring rules:
#   - key-down/key-up pairs are separated by >=3 boundaries so the press and
#     release never land in the same frame's event drain (the game drains ALL
#     queued events once per frame; a same-drain press+release pair cancels,
#     e.g. 'p' would fire nothing).
#   - inputs are injected only at boundaries (never mid-frame), so each event
#     lands in the quiet tail of the 62.5ms frame period.
#
# Run:
#   ./obj/harness --seed 12345 --script test/harness/scripts/session.script \
#                 --out <dir> --hiscore test/harness/fixtures/hiScore.nul.data

1    capture help          # initial screen IS the help screen pre-refactor

3    keydown s             # start game
6    keyup s
40   capture start

# --- engagement 1: rotate left, thrust, two shots
50   keydown e
54   keyup e
60   keydown o
74   keyup o
80   keydown p
84   keyup p
95   keydown p
99   keyup p
120  capture gp1

# --- engagement 2: rotate right, thrust, shot
130  keydown r
134  keyup r
140  keydown o
154  keyup o
160  keydown p
164  keyup p
200  capture gp2

# --- engagement 3: hyperspace (seeded random re-entry)
210  keydown space
214  keyup space
240  capture gp3

# --- engagement 4: fire volley while thrusting
250  keydown o
268  keyup o
270  keydown p
274  keyup p
290  keydown p
294  keyup p
310  keydown p
314  keyup p
340  capture gp4

# --- engagement 5: long thrust + rotate
350  keydown e
356  keyup e
360  keydown o
390  keyup o
400  capture gp5

# --- coast: idle ship dies to seeded rocks/saucers (last life by ~b1150,
#     cf. gameover.script derivation); periodic checkpoints
600  capture gp6
800  capture gp7
1000 capture gp8
1200 capture gp9
1400 capture gp10
1700 capture hiscore        # game-over/hi-score screen (byte-stable >= b1200)

1720 keydown q              # quit from the hi-score screen -> clean exit
1724 keyup q
exit
